  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ROADS - Food and Nutrition Security</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main gaol of the the program is to improve the food and  nutrition security, especially reducing malnu nutrition among child under 5 years hold and women.  The Programme&#x2019;s nutrition approach is focused on investments into malnutrition prevention activities, improving access to water, sanitation and hygiene and improving district coordination of nutrition interventions. This includes supporting improved access to and availability of food through support for nutrition-sensitive agricultural production and market access and capacity building on food conservation and storage techniques. Availability of nutritious food throughout the year is a challenge in the target districts, which exacerbates the promotion of poor eating habits.
To promote sustainablefood and nutrition security,the Programme will increase the capacity of small-scale farmers to use smart agricultural techniques to produce nutritious food allyear round. This will be done by implementing targeted interventions to support farmers associations to adopt production plants focused on year-round and diverse production for sale and consumption, at same time building their capacity, through training and support in equipment for food conservation, post-harvest management and improved storage systems. In addition, nutrition education interventions will increase the knowledge and understanding of how smallholder households can make use of local produce to improve nutrition, by changing the prevalent food preparation and eating habits.
The Programme will support health centres to deliver the nutritional packages into the target communities through Community Health Workers and will strengthen coordination mechanisms for nutrition at the district level. The Programme will support training to the district health authorities on gender sensitive nutrition services,community led and driven health and nutrition services, and will support the health system to equip their personnel with key material for referral (for example register sheets, child measurement type, etc. that normally run out of stock and prevent services from being performed by health worker and community health workers), and support with having meetings with community leaders. Where casesof malnutrition are identified by the Programme,these will be referred to the health centres and relevant health services in the region.</narrative>
  </description>
